cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this reproducibility package, please cite it and the associated manuscript."
type: dataset
title: "Reproducibility package for a methodological appraisal of a Chinese expert consensus on spinal cord stimulation for diabetic foot"
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-20
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility package for a cross-sectional methodological appraisal of one published Chinese
  expert consensus on spinal cord stimulation for diabetic foot. Contains AGREE II and GRADE
  dual-appraiser scores, agreement statistics, a RIGHT reporting checklist, a source-claim
  verification audit, the clean manuscript and submission docx, computation scripts and a
  SHA-256 MANIFEST. All appraisal data are public; no identifiable human data are included.
authors:
  - family-names: Yang
    given-names: Yongxin
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-9698-6552"
    affiliation: "The Second Affiliated Hospital of Fujian University of Traditional Chinese Medicine, Fuzhou, Fujian 350003, China"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/yyx-4113/neuromodulation-limb-salvage-diabetic-foot"
keywords:
  - diabetic foot
  - spinal cord stimulation
  - clinical practice guideline
  - AGREE II
  - RIGHT
  - GRADE
  - methodological appraisal
  - reproducibility
